From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dspark: request-local measured verification policy

Use attributed per-request feedback to blend measured output/time with
prefix-acceptance predictions. Retain the selected width between decisions,
require a gain and uncertainty margin, and grow at most one width per step.
Manual spec_k takes priority. The existing enable_adaptive_verification
switch selects the CPU policy on DeepSeek V4.1; other models retain the GPU
allocator. Production has no hot loader. History decay is configurable.

